@startuml node-layouts
' ============================================================================
' node-layouts.puml — the adaptive ART node tiers (byte keys), grow with fan-out.
' Source of truth: src/persistent_artrie/nodes/{node4,node16,node48,node256}.rs.
' Drawn as a CONTIGUOUS per-tier comparison table (tier · fan-out · layout columns)
' hosted in a floating note; rows share borders (no gaps). These are four DISTINCT
' node types compared by fan-out (named by tier, not byte offsets), so the table
' reads as a comparison — not a single contiguous structure. Full-cell color via
' Creole |<#hex>| cells, a light→dark blue progression per tier.
' Color key:  #E3F2FD Node4 · #BBDEFB Node16 · #90CAF9 Node48 · #64B5F6 Node256
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam TitleFontSize 15
skinparam noteFontSize 14
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #37474F
}

title Adaptive ART node tiers (byte keys) — the layout grows with fan-out

note as NL
|= tier |= fan-out |= layout · scan |
|<#E3F2FD> Node4 |<#E3F2FD> 1..4 |<#E3F2FD> parallel key[4] + child[4] · linear scan |
|<#BBDEFB> Node16 |<#BBDEFB> 5..16 |<#BBDEFB> key[16] + child[16] · SSE4.1 SIMD compare |
|<#90CAF9> Node48 |<#90CAF9> 17..48 |<#90CAF9> 256-byte index → 48 child slots (2 loads) |
|<#64B5F6> Node256 |<#64B5F6> 49..256 |<#64B5F6> direct 256-slot child array (O(1) index) |

Char / u64 keys keep native labels: inline → sorted → sparse-indexed,
and CharBucket at high fan-out (no 4 GB Node256 over u32).
end note

legend bottom
| Color | Tier |
|<#E3F2FD>| Node4 — inline keys, linear scan |
|<#BBDEFB>| Node16 — sorted keys, SIMD compare |
|<#90CAF9>| Node48 — byte→slot index |
|<#64B5F6>| Node256 — direct child array |
endlegend
@enduml
